      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Is this really needed on android-mainline or a GKI branch?\n\nYes, there is no possibility of moving this into a vendor space. The `NVME_HWMON` is a boolean used under [drivers/nvme/host/nvme.h](https://source.corp.google.com/h/android/kernel/common/+/android-mainline:drivers/nvme/host/nvme.h;l\u003d1220)\n\nThe `nvme.h` is included in the [`drivers/nvme/host/core.c`](https://source.corp.google.com/h/android/kernel/common/+/android-mainline:drivers/nvme/host/core.c;l\u003d27) file that is dependent on the [`CONFIG_NVME_CORE` option](https://source.corp.google.com/h/android/kernel/common/+/android-mainline:drivers/nvme/host/Makefile;l\u003d13), that is set to `y` in gki_defconfig.\n\nGiven the above - the `NVME_HWMON` option is resolved inside a GKI kernel, so setting it up as a vendor module won\u0027t take any effect.\n\nEnabling this config allows us to add support for full nvme temp monitoring from its sensors.",
      "parentUuid": "8d15bd65_3b87adbb",
